 "result_text": "`DateTime` objects now work in f-strings and `format()` with a format spec, the same way `datetime` does.\n\nI added a `__format__` method to `DateTime` in `src/DateTime/DateTime.py`. With an empty spec it returns `str(self)`, so plain `{now}` output doesn't change. With a spec it passes it to `strftime`.\n\nI ran one check, and it printed `18.10.2026 09:33|2026/10/18 09:33:34.219487 UTC`. That covers `{n:%-d.%-m.%Y %H:%M}` and plain `{n}`. I didn't run the test suite or add tests, as you asked.",
